# global-no-interp: Does the global action name no_interp load, with no assignment to the state (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: v@7=0.6 rows=11
# pc: ODE0058
# ruling: XPPAUT accepts no_interp as a third reserved action name next to arret and out_put. The run shows that it assigns nothing, since x is still 0.6 at t=0.6.
x'=1
x(0)=0
aux v=x
global 1 x-0.55 {no_interp=1}
@ total=1,dt=0.1,meth=euler
